# A MeshCore repeater, from the node sheet to its console.
#
# A repeater is a node you look after rather than talk to. Its sheet carries the three things
# only MeshCore asks of one - log in, its status, and which nodes it hears - and its conversation
# is its console: a message to it is a command it runs for its admin, and its reply is the next
# bubble. The compose sheet lists its commands where the quick replies would be, because the
# Brick has no keyboard worth typing `get advert.interval` on.
#
# The Nodes list has one row before its first node - the chip bar (MESH_UI_NODES_LEAD_ROWS) - so
# a node's row is its index in the demo roster plus one. Echo Repeater is seeds[5] and row 6.

scene demo
clock 2026-01-15 12:00
protocol meshcore
repeater ECHO
tab nodes
key down 6
key a
hold 800

# Into the sheet, and down to its last three verbs: log in, status, neighbours.
key a
hold 1200
key down 6
hold 1600

# Back up to Message, which opens its conversation - and A there raises the compose sheet:
# Commands, not Quick replies.
key up 9
key a
hold 900
key a
hold 1600
key down
hold 900
key a
message out ECHO ver
hold 700
# No ack comes for a command: its reply is the answer, and settles it.
ack delivered
message in ECHO v1.17.1 (Build: 14-Aug-2026)
hold 2000
